course: dictionary
lesson: 1445
title: Words with two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. A carton is a box made of cardboard or plastic, like an egg carton. It can also mean the amount the box holds, as in «a carton of juice».
explain: Look at the words around it. «Then it goes into cartons and bottles and back into the cold, all the way to your fridge.» The bottles and the fridge tell you that a carton here is the box itself, something you can put in a cold place.
explain: Now try your meaning in the sentence. «So nobody finds an empty carton in the morning» only works with the box meaning, because an empty box is what you find. Swap in the meaning and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A carton is a box made of cardboard or plastic.
fact: «A carton of juice» means the amount the box holds.
fact: A juice carton is made of layers of paper, plastic and foil, which keep light and air out.
fact: Because of those layers, a juice carton cannot be recycled like plain paper with the newspapers.
fact: The words around a word, its context, show you which meaning the writer wants.
exercise: «Then it goes into cartons and bottles and back into the cold, all the way to your fridge.» In this sentence, what is a carton? | A kind of cold food | A bottle with a lid | An amount of juice | *A box made of cardboard or plastic
exercise: What does carton mean in the phrase «a carton of juice»? | A kind of paper | *The amount the box holds | A box made of cardboard | A cold shop that sells juice
exercise: Ella says a carton must always be made of paper. What is the right answer? | It is always a bottle | It is always full of juice | It must always be made of paper | *It can be made of cardboard or plastic
test: «The golden rule of a best buy is to compare the same amount: four juice cartons of 250 ml at 40p make a litre for £1.60.» Here, carton means | *The amount the carton holds | A shop that sells milk | A plastic box with no juice in it | A bottle with a lid
test: Which phrase uses carton to mean the box itself? | a carton of 250 ml | a carton of cold milk | *an empty milk carton | a carton of juice
exam: «For example, a boy in Auckland uses the last of the milk and writes «milk» on the shopping list, so nobody finds an empty carton in the morning.» What does carton mean here? | *The box itself | The amount of milk the box holds | A list of things to buy | A shop in Auckland
